// Opt-in type check for the console's JavaScript. Nothing is compiled and
// nothing is shipped: `tsc` reads the same files the page inlines and reports
// what it can prove wrong. Not wired into `run.sh`, because that would put a
// TypeScript download in a test suite that today needs only node — adopt it
// when you want it:
//
//     npx -p typescript@5 tsc -p velstra-cloud-console/tests/tsconfig.checkjs.json
//
// It found two real defects on 2026-09-06: a duplicated key in the label map,
// and `const status` shadowing `window.status`, which accounted for thirty of
// the fifty-three messages on its own. The sixteen that remain are missing
// annotations, not defects — `$()` returns an HTMLElement and the call sites
// know it is an input, `SCHEMA` is injected by the page, and `openForm` takes
// two optional fields it has never been told are optional.
{
  "compilerOptions": {
    "allowJs": true,
    "checkJs": true,
    "noEmit": true,
    "target": "ES2022",
    "lib": [
      "ES2022",
      "DOM",
      "DOM.Iterable"
    ],
    "strict": false,
    "module": "none"
  },
  "include": [
    "../src/assets/*.js"
  ]
}
